    {
      "audit": {
        "path": "E:/Samplinglib/research-wiki/semantic-roundtrip/audits/ASTIS-RT-20261008-L2PositiveComplexLift.json",
        "bytes": 33308,
        "lf_bytes": 33308,
        "raw_sha256": "7064b18071ec0ad23deaf3b8ddf77b27b4e299895bf85a3d9a30e3ce521448e0",
        "lf_sha256": "7064b18071ec0ad23deaf3b8ddf77b27b4e299895bf85a3d9a30e3ce521448e0"
      },
      "review": {
        "path": "E:/Samplinglib/runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-real-complex-lift60/source-review60/source.0.review.json",
        "bytes": 4887,
        "lf_bytes": 4887,
        "raw_sha256": "e0bb8d3be878ebc4ff794ac11f48814c528843d60ce596afaaaca22ccddad225",
        "lf_sha256": "e0bb8d3be878ebc4ff794ac11f48814c528843d60ce596afaaaca22ccddad225"
      },
      "native_verdict": "equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "native_binding": "ff30df57cfba3b7c73945d63d9d4e0083c001f24322cf9489636c17e9144b97e",
      "canonical_audit": {
        "id": "ASTIS-RT-20261008-L2PositiveComplexLift",
        "state": "accepted",
        "source": {
          "source_id": "companion-background:l2-real-complex-positive-lift",
          "anchor": "Appendix D.1 real Hilbert conventions and positive square-root background; B.10-B.11 actual all-macro square-root prerequisite, attributed ASTIS complexification completion, not a printed paper theorem.",
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A4",
          "original_text": "Attributed ASTIS-authored background completion, not a verbatim numbered paper theorem.\nLet Ω be an arbitrary measurable space, μ any measure, and D a bounded positive real-linear endomorphism of L²(μ;ℝ). Positivity includes selfadjointness. Define the actual quotient maps ιu=u+0i, Rg=Re g, Qg=Im g and Cg=conj(g) via Mathlib compLpL. The embedding preserves norm: ‖ιu‖=‖u‖ for every u, and its full range is exactly the fixed space of C: Cg=g iff there exists u with ιu=g. There exists a bounded complex-linear positive operator Dc on L²(μ;ℂ), with for every g, Dc g=ιD(Rg)+iιD(Qg), for every real u, Dc(ιu)=ι(Du), and for every complex g, C(Dc g)=Dc(Cg). No root or inverse is asserted.\nExact source anchor: Appendix D.1 real Hilbert conventions and positive square-root background; B.10-B.11 actual all-macro square-root prerequisite, attributed ASTIS complexification completion, not a printed paper theorem.\nSource-route distinction: Attributed ASTIS complexification background completion supporting the real Appendix D/B.10-B.11 route. Printed B.5 joint block P/U proof and scalar actual-T route are distinguished by the independently reconstructed source graph; this lift is not a printed main theorem or Γ.\nRemaining: No root, real descent of complex CFC root, uniqueness, Gamma0/B15/B16, weakH1/dynamics/main/error/querycost/composition, paper or Goal closure.",
          "text_sha256": "63bc9f6efe957b8daa08b51f4246ad32875d4fb73d5eb1b6fdef4e2a15c2fe9f"
        },
        "lean": {
          "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.L2RealComplexOperator.exists_positive_complex_lift",
          "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/Measure/L2RealComplexOperator.lean",
          "statement": "\n    {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (μ : Measure Ω)\n    (D : Lp ℝ 2 μ →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 μ) (hD : D.IsPositive) :\n    let ι : Lp ℝ 2 μ →L[ℝ] Lp ℂ 2 μ := Complex.ofRealCLM.compLpL 2 μ\n    let R : Lp ℂ 2 μ →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 μ := Complex.reCLM.compLpL 2 μ\n    let Q : Lp ℂ 2 μ →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 μ := Complex.imCLM.compLpL 2 μ\n    let C : Lp ℂ 2 μ →L[ℝ] Lp ℂ 2 μ := Complex.conjCLE.toContinuousLinearMap.compLpL 2 μ\n    (∀ u : Lp ℝ 2 μ, ‖ι u‖ = ‖u‖) ∧\n    (∀ g : Lp ℂ 2 μ, C g = g ↔ ∃ u : Lp ℝ 2 μ, ι u = g) ∧\n    ∃ Dc : Lp ℂ 2 μ →L[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 μ,\n      Dc.IsPositive ∧\n      (∀ g : Lp ℂ 2 μ, Dc g = ι (D (R g)) + Complex.I • ι (D (Q g))) ∧\n      (∀ u : Lp ℝ 2 μ, Dc (ι u) = ι (D u)) ∧\n      (∀ g : Lp ℂ 2 μ, C (Dc g) = Dc (C g))",
          "statement_sha256": "e16622012af861a3c37f587bb557107d7484fdda04329b73a3f1671718920c3f",
          "compiled": true,
          "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
          "decoder_context": [
            "Lp with exponent 2 denotes AE equivalence classes of measurable square-integrable functions over the displayed measure. Its real/complex Hilbert structure is the integral inner product. No finiteness or probability property of the measure is assumed.",
            "compLpL lifts the displayed bounded scalar continuous linear map to the same quotient function spaces; ofReal, re, im and conj act pointwise almost everywhere. The conjugation map is real linear and is not operator adjoint.",
            "D.IsPositive means the bounded real operator is selfadjoint and its quadratic form is nonnegative. Endomorphism multiplication denotes composition. Norm preservation and the full conjugation-fixed range are conclusions."
          ],
