            "anchor": "Appendix D.1 real Hilbert conventions and positive square-root background; B.10-B.11 actual all-macro square-root prerequisite, attributed ASTIS complexification completion, not a printed paper theorem.",
            "wording_status": "faithful paraphrase",
            "attribution": "Attributed ASTIS background completion supporting Fan Chen, Sinho Chewi, Jianfeng Lu and Matthew S. Zhang real positive-root prerequisite. This exact complexification is ASTIS-authored and is not a printed Γ/main theorem."
          },
          "statement": "Let Ω be an arbitrary measurable space, μ any measure, and D a bounded positive real-linear endomorphism of L²(μ;ℝ). Positivity includes selfadjointness. Define the actual quotient maps ιu=u+0i, Rg=Re g, Qg=Im g and Cg=conj(g) via Mathlib compLpL. The embedding preserves norm: ‖ιu‖=‖u‖ for every u, and its full range is exactly the fixed space of C: Cg=g iff there exists u with ιu=g. There exists a bounded complex-linear positive operator Dc on L²(μ;ℂ), with for every g, Dc g=ιD(Rg)+iιD(Qg), for every real u, Dc(ιu)=ι(Du), and for every complex g, C(Dc g)=Dc(Cg). No root or inverse is asserted.",
