            ],
            "lean_statement": "Let Ω be an arbitrary measurable space, μ any measure, and D a bounded positive real-linear endomorphism of L²(μ;ℝ). Positivity includes selfadjointness. Define the actual quotient maps ιu=u+0i, Rg=Re g, Qg=Im g and Cg=conj(g) via Mathlib compLpL. The embedding preserves norm: ‖ιu‖=‖u‖ for every u, and its full range is exactly the fixed space of C: Cg=g iff there exists u with ιu=g. There exists a bounded complex-linear positive operator Dc on L²(μ;ℂ), with for every g, Dc g=ιD(Rg)+iιD(Qg), for every real u, Dc(ιu)=ι(Du), and for every complex g, C(Dc g)=Dc(Cg). No root or inverse is asserted.",
