      "native_verdict": "equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "native_binding": "92c9a4af22df1d3aaccaf366796301be83c39e8188a52ce0f4d2440cbce87228",
      "canonical_audit": {
        "id": "ASTIS-RT-20261008-PBPSPositiveDefectComplexLift",
        "state": "accepted",
        "source": {
          "source_id": "companion-background:pbps-positive-defect-complex-lift",
          "anchor": "Appendix D.1 real Hilbert conventions and positive square-root background; B.10-B.11 actual all-macro square-root prerequisite, attributed ASTIS complexification completion, not a printed paper theorem.",
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A2",
          "original_text": "Attributed ASTIS-authored background completion, not a verbatim numbered paper theorem.\nLet E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including the explicit rank-zero extension. Let V:E→ℝ be C², let 0<α≤β, and assume α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v. Assume η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ(dx) proportional to exp(−V(x))dx, J as the law of (X,X+√η Z) for independent X∼μ,Z∼N(0,I), ν=J.snd, and Λ as the law of (Y,2X−Y) under J. The laws μ,J,ν are probabilities. There exists a Markov kernel S with, for every y, S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)), Λ.IsCondKernel S, Λ.fst=ν and Λ.snd=ν. There exists a selfadjoint bounded T on L²(ν;ℝ) such that for every u, ‖Tu‖≤‖u‖, Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx) ν-almost everywhere, and ∫Tu dν=∫u dν. Set D=I−T²; this exact full-domain squared defect is positive. Define the actual quotient maps ιu=u+0i, Rg=Re g, Qg=Im g and Cg=conj(g). Then ι preserves norm, Cg=g iff g=ιu for some real u, and there exists a bounded complex-linear positive Dc on L²(ν;ℂ) such that Dc g=ιD(Rg)+iιD(Qg), Dc(ιu)=ι(Du), and C(Dc g)=Dc(Cg), universally on their displayed domains. The operator T, positivity, kernel/law certificates and Dc are produced conclusions. No real Γ/root/descent/inverse is asserted.\nExact source anchor: Appendix D.1 real Hilbert conventions and positive square-root background; B.10-B.11 actual all-macro square-root prerequisite, attributed ASTIS complexification completion, not a printed paper theorem.\nSource-route distinction: Attributed ASTIS complexification background completion supporting the real Appendix D/B.10-B.11 route. Printed B.5 joint block P/U proof and scalar actual-T route are distinguished by the independently reconstructed source graph; this lift is not a printed main theorem or Γ.\nRemaining: No root, real descent of complex CFC root, uniqueness, Gamma0/B15/B16, weakH1/dynamics/main/error/querycost/composition, paper or Goal closure.",
          "text_sha256": "cb9b0c3e5e2e7453dbb1620c59c137e0079120e69a7cda14933878cf263ead33"
        },
        "lean": {
          "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.DefectComplexLift.actual_positive_defect_complex_lift",
          "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/DefectComplexLift.lean",
          "statement": "\n    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    {V : E → ℝ} {α β : ℝ≥0} {η : ℝ}\n    (hα : 0 < (α : ℝ)) (hαβ : α ≤ β) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E,\n      (α : ℝ)*‖v‖^2 ≤ (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ∧\n      (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ≤ (β : ℝ)*‖v‖^2)\n    (hη : 0 < η) (hβη : (β : ℝ)*η ≤ 1) :\n    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n    let J := (μ.prod (stdGaussian E)).map\n      (fun p : E × E => (p.1,p.1+Real.sqrt η • p.2))\n    let ν := J.snd\n    let Λ := J.map (fun p : E × E => (p.2,(2 : ℝ) • p.1-p.2))\n    let ι : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℂ 2 ν := Complex.ofRealCLM.compLpL 2 ν\n    let R : Lp ℂ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν := Complex.reCLM.compLpL 2 ν\n    let Q : Lp ℂ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν := Complex.imCLM.compLpL 2 ν\n    let C : Lp ℂ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℂ 2 ν := Complex.conjCLE.toContinuousLinearMap.compLpL 2 ν\n    IsProbabilityMeasure μ ∧ IsProbabilityMeasure J ∧ IsProbabilityMeasure ν ∧\n    ∃ S : Kernel E E, IsMarkovKernel S ∧\n      (∀ y, S y = (volume : Measure E).tilted\n        (fun x => -V ((1/2 : ℝ) • (y+x)) - ‖y-x‖^2/(8*η))) ∧\n      Λ.IsCondKernel S ∧ Λ.fst = ν ∧ Λ.snd = ν ∧\n      ∃ T : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν,\n        IsSelfAdjoint T ∧\n        (∀ u : Lp ℝ 2 ν, ‖T u‖ ≤ ‖u‖ ∧\n          (T u : E → ℝ) =ᵐ[ν] (fun y => ∫ x, u x ∂S y) ∧\n          (∫ y, T u y ∂ν) = ∫ y, u y ∂ν) ∧\n        ((1 : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν)-T*T).IsPositive ∧\n        (∀ u : Lp ℝ 2 ν, ‖ι u‖ = ‖u‖) ∧\n        (∀ g : Lp ℂ 2 ν, C g = g ↔ ∃ u : Lp ℝ 2 ν, ι u = g) ∧\n        ∃ Dc : Lp ℂ 2 ν →L[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 ν,\n          Dc.IsPositive ∧\n          (∀ g : Lp ℂ 2 ν, Dc g =\n            ι (((1 : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν)-T*T) (R g)) +\n            Complex.I • ι (((1 : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν)-T*T) (Q g))) ∧\n          (∀ u : Lp ℝ 2 ν, Dc (ι u) = ι (((1 : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν)-T*T) u)) ∧\n          (∀ g : Lp ℂ 2 ν, C (Dc g) = Dc (C g))",
          "statement_sha256": "967721ee8c829b9e5f0db17c71ac28540efccc0345d212e491f680e18f0739d1",
          "compiled": true,
          "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
          "decoder_context": [
            "The underlying base is a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including zero dimension. The displayed potential is C2 with the two global Hessian bounds; positive ordered curvature and positive capped step are the entire analytic hypotheses.",
            "Measure.tilted denotes normalized exponential tilting. The displayed joint is the pushforward of an independent product with the standard Gaussian; the marginal is its second-coordinate law. Kernel normalization, Markov measurability, disintegration and both stationary marginals are produced conclusions.",
            "Lp exponent 2 denotes AE square-integrable quotient functions on the displayed marginal. Conditional operator action is an AE conclusion, while the displayed kernel density identity holds at every state. Operator multiplication is composition.",
            "compLpL lifts the displayed scalar embedding/real part/imaginary part/pointwise conjugation to quotient classes. Positivity includes selfadjointness. The real operator and its positive squared defect are produced internally; the complex positive lift is a conclusion. No square root or inverse is asserted."
          ],
